  <div id="sutta">
  
    <h4 id="thag6.6" class="h1">Thag 6:6  Sappadāsa</h4>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>Twenty five years since my going forth,</p>
              <p>and no peace of awareness</p>
              <p>—not a finger-snap’s worth—</p>
              <p class="v2">attained.</p>
              <p>Having gained no oneness of mind,</p>
              <p>I was wracked with lust.</p>
              <p>Wailing, with my arms upheld,</p>
              <p>I ran amok from my dwelling—</p>
              <p>“Or… or shall I take the knife?</p>
              <p>What’s the use of life to me?</p>
              <p>If I were to renounce the training,</p>
              <p>what sort of death would I have?”</p>
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>So, taking a razor,</p>
                <p>I sat down on a bed.</p>
                <p>And there was the razor,</p>
                <p>placed ready to cut my own vein,</p>
                <p class="v2">when apt attention arose in me,</p>
                <p>the drawbacks appeared,</p>
                <p class="v2">disenchantment stood</p>
                <p class="v2">at an even keel:</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>With that, my heart was released.</p>
                <p>See the Dhamma’s true rightness!</p>
                <p>The three knowledges</p>
                <p>have been attained;</p>
                <p>the Awakened One’s bidding,</p>
                <p class="v4">done.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
            </div><!--end verse-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
